# Secrets
# .env itself is tracked on purpose — Lovable manages it and it holds only
# publishable values (Supabase URL, project id, anon key), all of which ship
# in the browser bundle anyway.
#
# ANY REAL SECRET GOES IN .env.local, WHICH IS NEVER COMMITTED.
# That means the Unsplash access key, Stripe secret key, service_role key,
# and anything else that must not be public. Vite loads .env.local after .env
# and it takes precedence, so it also works for overriding values locally.
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production

# Wrangler / Cloudflare
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

